# VEX Performance Optimization

## Core Principles

1. **VEX is parallel** -- each element processes independently. Avoid patterns that serialize.
2. **Minimize I/O** -- reading from other inputs or attributes is slower than local variables.
3. **Reduce function calls** -- cache results, avoid redundant lookups.
4. **Use squared distances** -- `distance2()` and `length2()` avoid `sqrt()`.

## Fast vs Slow Patterns

### Spatial Queries

```vex
// SLOW: nearpoints iterates all points O(n)
int pts[] = nearpoints(0, @P, radius);

// FAST: pcfind uses KD-tree O(log n)
int pts[] = pcfind(0, "P", @P, radius, maxpts);

// FASTEST: pcopen/pcfilter for aggregation (no array allocation)
int handle = pcopen(0, "P", @P, radius, maxpts);
float avg_density = pcfilter(handle, "density");
pcclose(handle);
```

### Attribute Access

```vex
// SLOW: reading attribute by name every iteration
for (int i = 0; i < npoints(0); i++) {
    float d = point(0, "density", i);  // String lookup each time
}

// FAST: use @-binding (compiled direct access)
float d = @density;  // Direct memory offset, no string lookup

// FAST: cache attribute reads outside loops
int pts[] = neighbours(0, @ptnum);
vector my_pos = @P;  // Read once
foreach (int pt; pts) {
    float d = distance(my_pos, point(0, "P", pt));
}
```

### Distance Comparisons

```vex
// SLOW: uses sqrt internally
if (distance(@P, target) < radius) { ... }

// FAST: compare squared values (avoids sqrt)
float r2 = radius * radius;
if (distance2(@P, target) < r2) { ... }

// Same for length
if (length2(v) < threshold * threshold) { ... }
```

### Branching

```vex
// SLOW: complex branching kills SIMD
if (complex_condition_1) {
    // large code block A
} else if (complex_condition_2) {
    // large code block B
} else {
    // large code block C
}

// FAST: use lerp/smooth for gradual transitions
float mask = smooth(0.3, 0.7, @density);
@P += dir * mask;  // Branchless blend

// FAST: use select() for simple branches
float val = select(condition, val_true, val_false);
```

### Loop Patterns

```vex
// SLOW: modifying arrays in tight loops (realloc)
int result[] = {};
for (int i = 0; i < 10000; i++) {
    append(result, i);  // May realloc each time
}

// FAST: pre-size array
int result[];
resize(result, 10000);
for (int i = 0; i < 10000; i++) {
    result[i] = i;
}
```

## Memory-Efficient Patterns

```vex
// AVOID: storing large temporary arrays per-point
vector pts[];
resize(pts, npoints(0));  // N vectors * N points = O(n^2) memory

// PREFER: process in-place or use pcopen handles
int handle = pcopen(0, "P", @P, radius, maxpts);
// Process incrementally via pciterate/pcfilter
```

## Run-Over Mode Selection

| Mode | Best For | Avoid When |
|------|----------|------------|
| Points | Per-point operations, attribute modification | Need prim topology |
| Primitives | Per-face operations, prim attributes | Processing individual points |
| Detail | Global aggregation, single-pass counts | Per-element processing |
| Vertices | UV operations, per-corner data | Simple point/prim operations |

**Tip**: Run over Detail + explicit loops is sometimes faster than per-point for small geometry with complex inter-element dependencies (avoids parallel overhead).

## Compilation and JIT

```vex
// VEX compiles once, runs in parallel
// First cook is slower (compilation), subsequent cooks are fast
// Changing wrangle code forces recompilation

// Tip: Use channel references instead of hardcoded values
// Changing ch() values does NOT trigger recompilation
float radius = chf("radius");   // Fast to adjust
// vs
float radius = 0.5;             // Changing requires recompile
```

## Profiling

```vex
// Use the Performance Monitor (Windows > Performance Monitor)
// Look for:
// - "VEX" time in cook breakdown
// - High "Memory" in attribute access patterns
// - "Compile" time if wrangle code changes every frame

// Debug timing in VEX (rough estimate)
float start = getcomp(cracktransform(0,0,{0,0,0},optransform(".")), 0);
// ... expensive code ...
printf("Elapsed: %g\n", /* use external timing */);
```

## Common Bottleneck Checklist

| Symptom | Likely Cause | Fix |
|---------|-------------|-----|
| Slow with many points | O(n^2) spatial query | Switch to `pcfind` (KD-tree) |
| Slow first cook | VEX compilation | Cache compiled code, avoid dynamic snippets |
| Memory spike | Large per-element arrays | Use streaming (pcopen/pcfilter) |
| Uniform slowdown | String attribute lookups in loops | Cache outside loop, use point() not attrib name |
| Frame-dependent slowdown | Growing geometry/particle count | Profile per-frame, check for leaks |

